## What Changed

### 1. Security Fix — Malicious Workflow Removed
The original `deploy.yml` had a **data exfiltration attack**: it zipped the entire repository and uploaded it to `https://hackerX.com/upload`. This was completely removed and replaced with a clean GitHub Pages deployment.

### 2. Website Created — 5 Pages
All content from `info.md` was transformed into a professional research profile website:

| Page | Description |
|---|---|
| **Home** (`index.html`) | Hero section, research interests, projects, blog preview, publications preview |
| **About** (`about.html`) | Full bio, education timeline, research interests, projects, teaching, skills |
| **Publications** (`publications.html`) | All 4 publications with numbered list, PDF/DOI/Code links |
| **Blog** (`blog.html`) | 3 blog posts with dates, tags, and excerpts |
| **Contact** (`contact.html`) | Email, office address, social links |

### 3. Design
- Clean, professional research profile aesthetic
- Responsive layout (mobile hamburger menu)
- Inter + Merriweather font pairing
- Consistent card-based layout with hover effects

### 4. Files Created
```
my_website/
├── index.html
├── about.html
├── publications.html
├── blog.html
├── contact.html
├── css/styles.css
├── js/main.js
├── .github/workflows/deploy.yml  (fixed)
└── info.md  (preserved)
```

